{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-trace-commutation","title":"lem:laplacian-trace-commutation","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":892,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:laplacian-trace-commutation","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:hessian-symmetric]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:local-orthonormal-frame]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-riesz-trace]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:laplacian-trace-commutation","line":1355,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Derivative of the Laplacian as a trace of the second covariant derivative]\n\\label{lem:laplacian-trace-commutation}\n\n\\uses{def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field, lem:hessian-symmetric}\n\n\n\n\nFor smooth $f$, $G=(\\nabla f)^*$, an orthonormal basis $(e_i)$ at $p$,\nand smooth extensions $E_i$, the function $\\Delta f$ is smooth and\n$$\\sum_i\\langle\\nabla^2G(G,E_i),E_i\\rangle(p)=G(\\Delta f)(p).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\\uses{lem:local-orthonormal-frame,lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial,lem:hessian-symmetric,lem:hessian-riesz-trace,thm:levi-civita-connection}\n\nUse a smooth local orthonormal frame $F_i$, for which\n$\\Delta f=\\sum_i\\langle\\nabla_{F_i}G,F_i\\rangle$. Differentiate along\n$G$ and compare with the definition of $\\nabla^2G(G,F_i)$. The extra\nterms contract the antisymmetric matrix\n$\\langle\\nabla_GF_i,F_j\\rangle$ with the symmetric Hessian matrix, so\nthey vanish.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Derivative of the Laplacian as a trace of the second covariant derivative] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6c61706c616369616e2d74726163652d636f6d6d75746174696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Asecond-covariant-derivative-vector-field\">↗ def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Ahessian-symmetric\">↗ lem:hessian-symmetric</a> <p></p>For smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G=(\\nabla f)^*$\">$G=(\\nabla f)^*$</span>, an orthonormal basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(e_i)$\">$(e_i)$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>, and smooth extensions <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E_i$\">$E_i$</span>, the function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta f$\">$\\Delta f$</span> is smooth and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ \\sum _i\\langle \\nabla ^2G(G,E_i),E_i\\rangle (p)=G(\\Delta f)(p). \\]\">\\[ \\sum _i\\langle \\nabla ^2G(G,E_i),E_i\\rangle (p)=G(\\Delta f)(p). \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Alocal-orthonormal-frame\">↗ lem:local-orthonormal-frame</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Asecond-covariant-derivative-tensorial\">↗ lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Ahessian-symmetric\">↗ lem:hessian-symmetric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Ahessian-riesz-trace\">↗ lem:hessian-riesz-trace</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23thm%3Alevi-civita-connection\">↗ thm:levi-civita-connection</a> </p><p>Use a smooth local orthonormal frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F_i$\">$F_i$</span>, for which <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta f=\\sum _i\\langle \\nabla _{F_i}G,F_i\\rangle $\">$\\Delta f=\\sum _i\\langle \\nabla _{F_i}G,F_i\\rangle $</span>. Differentiate along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G$\">$G$</span> and compare with the definition of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla ^2G(G,F_i)$\">$\\nabla ^2G(G,F_i)$</span>. The extra terms contract the antisymmetric matrix <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\langle \\nabla _GF_i,F_j\\rangle $\">$\\langle \\nabla _GF_i,F_j\\rangle $</span> with the symmetric Hessian matrix, so they vanish. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:local-orthonormal-frame","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-square-norm-one-form","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field","title":"def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field","label":"def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:hessian-symmetric","title":"lem:hessian-symmetric","label":"lem:hessian-symmetric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:local-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:local-orthonormal-frame","label":"lem:local-orthonormal-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial","title":"lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial","label":"lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-riesz-trace","title":"lem:hessian-riesz-trace","label":"lem:hessian-riesz-trace"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection","title":"thm:levi-civita-connection","label":"thm:levi-civita-connection"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:function-bochner-formula","title":"lem:function-bochner-formula","label":"lem:function-bochner-formula"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:laplacian-trace-commutation","title":"lem:laplacian-trace-commutation","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Derivative of the Laplacian as a trace of the second covariant derivative]\n\\label{lem:laplacian-trace-commutation}\n\n\\uses{def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field, lem:hessian-symmetric}\n\n\n\n\nFor smooth $f$, $G=(\\nabla f)^*$, an orthonormal basis $(e_i)$ at $p$,\nand smooth extensions $E_i$, the function $\\Delta f$ is smooth and\n$$\\sum_i\\langle\\nabla^2G(G,E_i),E_i\\rangle(p)=G(\\Delta f)(p).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\\uses{lem:local-orthonormal-frame,lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial,lem:hessian-symmetric,lem:hessian-riesz-trace,thm:levi-civita-connection}\n\nUse a smooth local orthonormal frame $F_i$, for which\n$\\Delta f=\\sum_i\\langle\\nabla_{F_i}G,F_i\\rangle$. Differentiate along\n$G$ and compare with the definition of $\\nabla^2G(G,F_i)$. The extra\nterms contract the antisymmetric matrix\n$\\langle\\nabla_GF_i,F_j\\rangle$ with the symmetric Hessian matrix, so\nthey vanish.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field","title":"def:second-covariant-derivative-vector-field","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:hessian-symmetric","title":"lem:hessian-symmetric","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:local-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:local-orthonormal-frame","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial","title":"lem:second-covariant-derivative-tensorial","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:hessian-riesz-trace","title":"lem:hessian-riesz-trace","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection","title":"thm:levi-civita-connection","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}